---
import StaticPage from '../layouts/StaticPage.astro';
import { SITE_NAME } from '../consts';
---

<StaticPage
  title="About"
  description={`About ${SITE_NAME}: an independent, automated-ready American news publishing platform.`}
  canonicalPath="/about/"
  updated="September 2026"
>
  <p>
    {SITE_NAME} is an independent American news publication built on a modern,
    static-first publishing engine. Our mission is to deliver fast, factual, and
    clearly-sourced coverage of the stories that shape life across the United
    States — from national politics and severe weather to product recalls,
    consumer affairs, and science.
  </p>

  <h2>How we are built</h2>
  <p>
    This website is generated as static HTML for maximum speed, accessibility, and
    search performance. Every story is stored as a structured article record with a
    consistent schema — headline, description, author, timestamps, hero image,
    body, source attribution, tags, and more. Homepage sections, category pages,
    related stories, and search-engine metadata are all derived automatically from
    that single source of truth.
  </p>

  <h2>Editorial independence</h2>
  <p>
    {SITE_NAME} is not affiliated with any political party, government agency, or
    commercial advertiser. Editorial decisions are made independently of
    advertising or sponsorship considerations. See our{' '}
    <a href="/editorial-policy/">Editorial Policy</a> for details.
  </p>

  <h2>How our articles are produced</h2>
  <p>
    Stories on this site are produced automatically from cited source material.
    Our official-source desks use National Weather Service alerts, CPSC and FDA
    recall notices, USGS earthquake data, and NASA / JPL / NOAA science releases.
    General News also uses cited publisher coverage. Articles identify their
    source and provide a link to the original coverage, alert, recall, or release
    when available. Our automated newsroom publishes source-driven articles
    without human intervention; see our{' '}
    <a href="/editorial-policy/">Editorial Policy</a> for details on how this
    works and the standards we follow.
  </p>

  <h2>Contact</h2>
  <p>
    Questions, corrections, or story tips? Visit our{' '}
    <a href="/contact/">Contact</a> page.
  </p>
</StaticPage>
